2.verdict:
I used 5 of the 15 allowed WebSearch calls, one per institution. Each was an EDEBO search (allowed_domains registry.edbo.gov.ua) whose summary covered the code, the Ukrainian name and the website together. No call was refused. Everything below is still a search-result lead; nothing is verified.

Lesya Ukrainka Volyn National University (1 search): EDEBO code 44, the Ukrainian name and vnu.edu.ua are confirmed, plus college 1041. The summary also gave the register e-mail [e-mail on vnu.edu.ua]. Two corrections: accreditationLicensing cites 'Law expert conclusion 0016/AC-23', which no source shows, and internationalAdmission names a 'General Information' page and misplaces 'Study in LUVNU'.

Luhansk State Medical University (1 search): EDEBO code 13, the name ДЗ «ЛДМУ» and lsmu.edu.ua are confirmed. The main correction is that the EDEBO summary now gives http://www.lsmu.edu.ua as the website, plus [e-mail on lsmu.edu.ua] and [phone number]. That contradicts domainOwnership, the officialWebsite note and the third conflicts item, and domainOwnership should not rest on a self-evaluation the university wrote. Two more corrections: medicalProgrammes names departments and a Postgraduate Faculty that no source shows, and internationalAdmission cites page titles that no source shows.

Andrei Krupynskyi Lviv Medical Academy (1 search): code 627, the full communal Ukrainian name, lma.edu.ua and the Doroshenka 70 address are confirmed. The register e-mail [e-mail on ukr.net] was also seen. Corrections:
- the English name conflict between EDEBO and Study in Ukraine should be classified as conflicting leads;
- the 1,800 USD fee is not tied to Nursing in the extract;
- 'sign the agreement' is not in the source;
- two urlsToCapture entries are not cited by any source.

Lviv Medical Institute / private ВПНЗ «ЛМУ» (1 search): code 1362, the Ukrainian name, medinstytut.lviv.ua, the Patona 22-A address, the founding date 04.03.2004 and director Гайдучок are confirmed. The summary also gave postcode 79040 and the register e-mail [e-mail on gmail.com], and it showed LNMU 121 blocked with successor 7314. Corrections:
- EDEBO gives an English name, 'Private higher education institution \"Lviv medical university\"', which contradicts officialNameEn 'none found';
- the subdomains in officialWebsite are not in any source;
- 'funded by individuals or legal entities' and 'originals on arrival' are not in the extracts;
- the 2021 'ТзОВ' document in conflicts is not cited;
- three urlsToCapture entries are not cited by any source.

Lviv Polytechnic National University (1 search): code 97, the Ukrainian name, lpnu.ua and Stepana Bandery 12 are confirmed. EDEBO also shows a second structural unit, IT college 6520 (itcollege.lviv.ua), which the registerListing value does not mention; that is not a contradiction. Corrections: the 'only' claim in medicalProgrammes, 'merged 2021-2024' in currentStatus, and a page title quoted in accreditationLicensing that the extract does not show.

Not reported as corrections:
- Several fields mark 'conflicts with record' but keep a source-strength classification: Volyn medicalProgrammes, Luhansk currentStatus, Krupynskyi medicalProgrammes, and the Lviv Medical Institute address difference. In each case the conflict is already documented in newVsRecord and the conflicts list.
- Lviv Polytechnic internationalAdmission says foreigners can study at bachelor's, master's and doctoral level, self-funded or under intergovernmental agreements. That comes from the existing record, not from the cited extracts.

No third-party fee is shown as official, and no contact detail comes from a non-official source. Krupynskyi's [e-mail on gmail.com] is a gmail address but comes from the official domain, and the note already flags it.
